    "message": "Answer frame reads while a save is being indexed\n\nA save moves the branch pointer before it indexes the new head. A read in\nbetween found the index stale and fell back to the legacy timeline file,\nwhich new Runs do not have, so earlier minutes failed with \"no checkpoint\nexists before requested minute\". Saved Checkpoints never change and a\nbranch only grows, so the index answers up to its head and the pointer's\nhead answers its own minute.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
